<title>EGYPT: IFC helping finance Egyptian tourist project.</title>
<headline>IFC helping finance Egyptian tourist project.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corporation (IFC), private-sector finance arm of the World Bank, said on Thursday it had agreed to contribute $25 million towards expanding a tourist complex on Egypt's Red Sea coast.</p>
<p>IFC will lend the private Egyptian company Orascom Projects and Tourisic Development (OPTD) $20 million and make an equity investment of $5 million on its own account in the project at El-Gouna, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>OPTD expects to spend more than $100 million on expanding the complex at El Gouna and the IFC's long-term loan will help restructure OPTD's short-term debt, it said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
